WHAT THIS FILE ESTABLISHES

  The console evidence for probe query one, the call-graph reachability query.
  This is the FOURTH and last of the four heap-bound JVM invocations this run
  records separately - the jimple2cpg frontend build, the importCpg verification
  load, the Stage 3 Joern runner, and this probe - and the only one of the four
  whose subject is a question about Joern rather than a question about Spark.

  It carries, in execution order: the preconditions that had to hold before the
  query was allowed to load the graph, the target surface the query addresses
  measured in the pinned tree rather than assumed, the exact command with its
  JDK major version and the heap it actually received recorded as three separate
  fields, every figure the query reported, the cross-checks against the two
  result files the query wrote, and the terminal transcript verbatim.

  The <nn>-<slug> in this file's name matches the query source exactly:
  queries/joern/01-callgraph-unguarded-driver-launch.sc.

  WHAT THIS FILE IS NOT. It is not a finding, and nothing in it is an assessment
  of Spark, of any Spark component or of any Spark configuration. It judges no
  finding - not real, not important, not a false positive, not a duplicate of
  another tool's - and it makes no comparison between tools. It contributes NO
  row to oss-scan-results/findings.json and writes nothing into
  harness/artifacts/raw/. Joern appears twice in this run by design: once as one
  of the nine scanned runners, and once as the subject of this probe. Nothing
  here is added to, merged with or compared against that runner's output, and no
  figure in this file is arithmetic over the two. Reading the double appearance
  as a duplication would corrupt both counts.

