PHASE 1 - THE PRECONDITIONS THAT HAD TO HOLD BEFORE THE QUERY LOADED THE GRAPH
================================================================================

  Six preconditions, each a halt if it fails. The graph must be the graph the
  record describes. The load mechanism must be importCpg, and the alternative
  must not appear even textually in the committed query source. The JVM must
  report major 21. The heap the query actually receives must be at or above the
  64 GiB floor, and the host must be shown to COMMIT that heap rather than
  merely reserve it. Nothing else may hold a 64 GB Joern process at the same
  time. And the setup-time smoke override must be unset.

